-- Two modules each declare an interface `Desc` with a method `desc`.  `ma`'s
-- carries a context over its parameter; `mb`'s carries none, and `mb.useB` calls
-- it.  `ma` is imported first, so its method-context row is in the table when
-- `mb`'s own same-spelled method is checked.  Expected, from mb's impl:
-- useB 20 = desc 20 + 1 = 20 * 2 + 1 = "41".
import method_context_samename_xmod.ma.{Show2}
import method_context_samename_xmod.mb.{useB}

main = println (useB 20)
